Now I have my references:
1. **GameDev.net — Swept AABB Collision Detection and Response** (https://gamedev.net/tutorials/_/technical/game-programming/swept-aabb-collision-detection-and-response-r3084/): rule — compute the first time of impact along the movement vector; resolve at that time with the surface normal; prevents tunneling.
2. **noonat — Intersection Tests in 2D** (https://noonat.github.io/intersect/): rule — for a static overlap, resolve along the axis of smallest overlap (hit.delta push-out); for a sweep, use hit.time to stop before contact. Also the "circle vs swept AABB" / "sweeping a circle through multiple objects" concept — take the earliest hit.
3. **Brian Semrau — Dealing with Ghost Collisions** (http://briansemrau.github.io/dealing-with-ghost-collisions/): rule — never resolve each overlapping piece of a shared surface independently with its own normal; ghost collisions (normal flips, double resolution) happen exactly there. For our case: one bounce per pass per axis; same-row seam = one surface.
